& Recreation Athletics Esports Washington DC School Spirit and Traditions Student Services News & Events Life After GU Career Preparedness Alumni Gallaudet Opportunities for Advancement and Learning (GOAL) Research and Innovation Visit Apply Link #2 Apply Give Request Info Gallaudet Athletics (opens in new window) Bison Shop (opens in new window) Youth Current Students Staff & Faculty Parents Alumni Learn ASL GOAL Search Search for: Directories Personnel Degrees Areas of Study Courses Events Popular Keywords Tuition Housing Academic Visit Financial Aid My Account Registrar Employment Alumni Athletics Library Commencement News Events Homecoming Student Life Tools & Resources Bison Shop Calendar Bus Shuttle E-mail MyGU Library Gallaudet Today Maps & Directions Workday Blackboard A-Z Index Type to filter offices Academic & Career Success Academic Affairs Access Control Alumni Association Alumni Relations Archives Arts and Humanities ASL and English Bilingualism ASL Connect Athletics & Intramurals Belonging & Engagement Buff and Blue Media Campus Design and Facilities Campus Events Campus Services Civic Leadership, Business and Social Change Counseling and Psychological Services Curriculum, Outreach, Resources, and Effectiveness Deaf Way Festivals Dean of the Faculty Development Office Education Abroad and International Fellowships Enrollment and Communications Family Engagement Coordinator Finance Financial Aid Gallaudet Opportunities for Advancement and Learning Gallaudet Press Graduate Admissions Graduate School Graduate Student Association Hearing and Speech Center Human Resources Human Services and Sciences Institutional Advancement Institutional Effectiveness and Certification Institutional Research Institutional Review Board International Relations Interpreting Services Kendall Demonstration Elementary School Language, Education, and Culture Laurent Clerc National Deaf Education Center Maguire Welcome Center Model Secondary School for the Deaf Multicultural Student Programs National Deaf Life Museum Office for Career Success Office of Arts, Culture, and Experience Office of International Affairs Office of Research and Innovation Office of the General Counsel Office of the President Office of the Registrar Operations Psychology Clinic Public Safety Real Estate Residence Life and Housing Science, Technology, Accessibility, Mathematics, and Public Health Strategic Planning & Integration Strategic Sourcing Student Accountability & Restorative Practices (SARP) Student Affairs Student Body Government Student Center Programs and Services Student Engagement and Leadership Student Financial Services Technology Services Undergraduate Admissions University Communications University Library Youth Programs Jump to a Section Overview Schools Departments News Faculty and Staff Information Contact Link #1 Contact Login Interfolio Academic Calendars Academic Affairs Research Center Library Faculty Governance GU / Dean of the Faculty Division Dean of the Faculty Hall Memorial Building S333 202-250-2405 (202) 651-5000 Email Link #1 Email Us Overview The Office of the Dean of the Faculty is dedicated to fostering a diverse and distinguished community of faculty at our university. Our goal is to provide faculty with the resources and support they need to conduct transformative research and teaching, engage across academic disciplines, and educate the next generation of leaders and innovators. We recruit, retain, and develop faculty in a range of disciplines across our five schools: 1) Human Services and Sciences, 2) Language, Education, and Culture, 3) Arts and Humanities, 4) Science, Technology, Accessibility, Mathematics, and Public Health, and 5) Civic Leadership, Business and Social Change. In addition to managing academic policies and procedures, the Dean of the Faculty is committed to establishing standards of conduct that foster a positive and respectful learning environment. If you are a current faculty member or are considering joining our community, we encourage you to contact us to learn more about available opportunities. We look forward to working with you and supporting your research, teaching, and professional development at our university. Academic Affairs Dean's List Schools Civic Leadership, Business and Social Change Science, Technology, Accessibility, Mathematics, and Public Health Language, Education, and Culture Human Services and Sciences Arts and Humanities Programs General Education Honors Program B.A. in Liberal Studies Self-Directed Major News Previous Next August 17, 2026 Education and IT programs welcome new faculty members More Link #1 Read More August 14, 2026 From Gallaudet to Brno: AHCP Cohort Presents Four Papers at ICCHP 2026 More Link #2 Read More August 14, 2026 Driven to help students thrive: Gallaudet’s newly tenured faculty More Link #3 Read More July 22, 2026 Remembering Catherine Moses, revered Social Work professor and advocate More Link #4 Read More June 24, 2026 ASL Signbank: New book explores a way to make signed words stay More Link #5 Read More June 17, 2026 AHCP program’s power showcased at inaugural DeafTech Conference More Link #6 Read More June 3, 2026 From partying to a PhD: keeping up with Reggie Bess More Link #7 Read More April 15, 2026 Gallaudet center advances access to care for Deaf communities More Link #8 Read More March 30, 2026 A new Deaf-centric debate series draws on deep roots More Link #9 Read More February 22, 2026 New STAMP-centered career fair provides future-forward training and career opportunities More Link #10 Read More February 22, 2026 More Link #11 Gallaudet Center makes trauma-informed care more available and accessible More Link #12 Read More February 13, 2026 Checking in with the Center for Black Deaf Studies More Link #13 Read More December 11, 2025 Q&A with Fulbright Distinguished Scholar, Dr. Teresa Blankmeyer Burke More Link #14 Read More December 11, 2025 Bringing families into Gallaudet’s fold More Link #15 Read More December 8, 2025 Strong showing by Gallaudet and the Clerc Center at national conference More Link #16 Read More December 8, 2025 Making the case: Gallaudet experts featured at first panel dedicated to Deaf people and criminal justice at national conference More Link #17 Read More December 1, 2025 Dripping with creativity More Link #18 Read More November 17, 2025 Public Health students zoom in on scooter and bike safety More Link #19 Read More November 5, 2025 “You matter.” New Interim Assistant Dean draws on career prioritizing students More Link #20 Read More October 24, 2025 Checking up on Gallaudet’s Public Health program More Link #21 Read More October 24, 2025 Math professor’s excellence recognized with Gallaudet’s first endowed professorship More Link #22 Read More October 13, 2025 Trio of talented artists inspires students this fall More Link #23 Read More September 28, 2025 Acclaimed alumni take students on a journey with new production: Q&A with James Caverly and Andrew Morrill More Link #24 Read More September 28, 2025 Meet this year’s Deaf Studies Incubator Fellows More Link #25 Read More September 4, 2025 Professor contributes to first comprehensive framework for AI interpreting More Link #26 Read More August 28, 2025 Gallaudet wins $4.5M award for new universal-AI graduate research traineeship program More Link #27 Read More August 18, 2025 Welcoming new graduate students to Gallaudet’s culture and language More Link #28 Read More August 6, 2025 Dr. Maribel Gárate-Estes named interim Dean of the Faculty More Link #29 Read More August 4, 2025 Summer interns harness AI for accessibility More Link #30 Read More July 23, 2025 Visiting researcher from Spain highlights sign language, Deaf experience in his films More Link #31 Read More June 24, 2025 Gallaudet experts drive accessibility of speech tech for deaf voices More Link #32 Read More May 8, 2025 Record number of honors capstone projects hone students’ creativity and research skills More Link #33 Read Mor