ional Deaf Life Museum Office for Career Success Office of Arts, Culture, and Experience Office of International Affairs Office of Research and Innovation Office of the General Counsel Office of the President Office of the Registrar Operations Psychology Clinic Public Safety Real Estate Residence Life and Housing Science, Technology, Accessibility, Mathematics, and Public Health Strategic Planning & Integration Strategic Sourcing Student Accountability & Restorative Practices (SARP) Student Affairs Student Body Government Student Center Programs and Services Student Engagement and Leadership Student Financial Services Technology Services Undergraduate Admissions University Communications University Library Youth Programs Jump to a Section Overview News Departments Programs Meet the Team Information FAQs Contact Link #1 Contact GU / Education Abroad and International Fellowships Academic & Career Success Education Abroad and International Fellowships Building 103 207 (202) 651-5135 Email Link #1 Email Us Overview Gallaudet’s Education Abroad and International Fellowships Office supports all students who wish to take classes, conduct research, or complete internships outside the United States. The office designs programs tailored to the unique needs and interests of the Gallaudet community while helping students find international experiences that deepen their cultural understanding. The benefits of studying abroad are endless in an increasingly globalized world. Studying abroad is often a differentiator for Gallaudet graduates seeking employment. Available programming varies from year to year. Explore our current offerings today. News September 3, 2026 Gallaudet goes to Ghana: Education Abroad launches its first program in Africa More Link #1 Read More June 8, 2026 Thirteen Gallaudet students win Gilman Scholarships in record application year More Link #2 Read More April 26, 2026 Education Abroad and International Fellowships Update More Link #3 Read More December 11, 2025 Q&A with Fulbright Distinguished Scholar, Dr. Teresa Blankmeyer Burke More Link #4 Read More Programs Fulbright Program Explore Gallaudet University's Fulbright Program for education abroad opportunities. Gain international experience, cultural exchange, and academic growth. Join us! Virtual Exchange – Collaborative Online International Learning (VE-COIL) Explore Gallaudet University's VE-Coil program, offering unique education abroad and international fellowship opportunities for students seeking global experiences. Meet the Team Robert Sanchez Dean, Academic and Career Success Fiona Grugan Education Abroad Manager Information What We Do in Education Abroad and International Fellowships Explore Gallaudet's Education Abroad and International Fellowships programs, designed to enhance global learning experiences and foster cultural exchange for students. More Link #5 More Contact Education Abroad and International Fellowships Building 103 | 207 abroad@gallaudet.edu (202) 651-5135 Monday 9:00 am-5:00 pm Tuesday 9:00 am-5:00 pm Wednesday 9:00 am-5:00 pm Thursday 9:00 am-5:00 pm Friday 9:00 am-5:00 pm Robert Sanchez Dean, Academic and Career Success Overview News Departments Programs Meet the Team Information FAQs Contact Link #2 Contact Back to Academic & Career Success Testimonial Let's Stay In Touch Join our mailing list to learn more about Gallaudet Visit Apply Link #3 Apply Give Request Information Footer Content Footer Content At a Glance Quick Facts University Leadership History & Traditions Accreditation Consumer Information Our 10-Year Vision: The Gallaudet Promise Annual Report of Achievements (ARA) The Signing Ecosystem Not Your Average University Our Community Directory MyGU Library & Archives Technology Support Interpreting Requests Health and Wellness Programs Workday Profile & Web Edits Bison Shop Visit Gallaudet Explore Our Campus Virtual Tour Maps & Directions Shuttle Bus Schedule Kellogg Conference Hotel Welcome Center National Deaf Life Museum Apple Guide Maps DeafSpace Engage Today Work at Gallaudet / Clerc Center Social Media Channels University Wide Events Data Requests Subscribe Gallaudet Today Magazine Giving at Gallaudet Gallaudet University Press Contact Us Financial Aid Human Resources Registrar’s Office Residence Life & Housing Safety & Security Undergraduate Admissions Graduate Admissions University Communications Clerc Center English Language Institute Gallaudet University, chartered in 1864, is a private university for deaf and hard of hearing students. YouTube Link Instagram Link Twitter Link Copyright © 2026 Gallaudet University. All rights reserved. Accessibility Anti-Discrimination Statement Cookie Consent Notice Privacy Policy File a Report Sitemap 800 Florida Avenue NE, Washington, D.C. 20002"
